   "design": "One maintained social map replaces binders and loose websites. The counselor searches it, and information packets are printed from it. Families can find services on an answer desk that quotes the social map, marked as AI, and anything about a client or a crisis goes to a person. Referral letters start from the counselor's spoken notes, with consent; the counselor corrects each one, and a validator flags risk statements not in the notes. Explaining, discussing the referral, the check, sending and the record note stay with the counselor.",
   "previous_blocker": "Service information was scattered, and every family question came to the counselor.",
   "enabler_now": "A maintained social map, an answer desk over it and spoken-note drafting.",
   "still_hard": "Services with waiting lists that change weekly.",
   "human_edge": "Choosing the service this client will actually go to.",
